Absolute Suite v@BUNDLE_VERSION@ Beta
=====================================

ALL-IN-ONE INSTALLER
--------------------

- Added one guided FOMOD for Absolute Control and the modular Absolute
  ecosystem.
- Kept Absolute Control required while making HOTAS, Power, Head Tracking, and
  Mouse Steering independently selectable.
- Preserved the exact standalone DLL and default-INI boundaries. No gameplay
  module is merged into the host.
- Added clear warnings for Power's shipped 1-4 preset shortcuts and
  AbsoluteZero's immediately active mouse-centering behavior.
- Added Absolute Control's native Head Pose calibration instruments, radial
  response rendering, and visible binding clearing.
- Added Absolute Head Tracking 1.0's asymmetric axes, recenter, manual-look
  bindings, constrained ballistic aim, and synchronized inner reticle.
- Added AbsoluteHOTAS 5.2's independent analog-aim deadzone.


RELEASE INTEGRITY
-----------------

- Added a machine-readable suite manifest containing component versions,
  source commits, installed paths, sizes, and SHA-256 hashes.
- Added deterministic archive ordering and timestamps.
- Excluded custom INIs, profiles, logs, PDBs, research artifacts, and retired
  Workbench descriptors.
- Added fail-closed package validation for exact contents and recorded hashes.


VALIDATION
----------

- Absolute Control native suites: 12/12 passed
- AbsoluteHOTAS native suites: 22/22 passed
- Absolute Power native suites: 9/9 passed
- Absolute Head Tracking native suites: 10/10 passed
- FOMOD and suite archive content validation: passed


KNOWN BETA BOUNDARIES
---------------------

- The all-in-one simplifies distribution; it does not change gameplay features
  or replace each module's standalone support boundary.
- This remains a beta across varied hardware and mod stacks; the qualified
  release artifacts and automated suites are the supported validation baseline.
